      ],
      "title": "Friendship was invented in 18th-century Scotland",
      "gist": "Work gives people impersonal, equal paths to dignity and respect that purely relational societies cannot offer, which is why losing work risks making society more clannish.",
      "question": "work and dignity — why does earning respect through a job make society freer than earning it through family or clan? (an argument from evidence and theory)",
      "sourceHeading": "Friendship was invented in 18th-century Scotland"
    },
    "n0083": {
